<code>assert \result != -1 => this.get(\result) == null == o;</code>

This assert statement checks that if the result of `lastIndexOf` is not -1 (meaning the element was found), then the element at the result index is null if and only if the input object `o` is null. This ensures that the method correctly identifies the last occurrence of a null element when `o` is null, and the last occurrence of a non-null element when `o` is non-null.--------------------<code>assert \result != -1 => this.get(\result) == null;</code>--------------------<code>assert (\result != -1 && this.get(\result) == null) => o == null;</code>--------------------